// A local the function reads before defining it holds caller state the
// prototype does not cover.  Ghidra usually names such a variable
// `unaff_<reg>` or `in_<location>`.  The lifter declares it as an ordinary
// uninitialized local, so the lifted function does not read the value the
// binary read; each such local is reported.
//
// The serializer records the fact as `live_in` on DECLARE_LOCAL and the flag
// decides when present, whatever the name.  JSON without the flag falls back
// to the naming convention and also requires that no operation writes the
// local, because a symbol can simply be called `in_count`.
//
//   legacy_unwritten  no flag; unaff_r4 and in_stack_00000004 never written   reported
//   legacy_written    no flag; in_count = a; return in_count                  not reported
//   flag_set          live_in true on a local named saved_state               reported
//   flag_clear        live_in false on in_total and unaff_r5                  not reported
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
